From 1111111111111111111111111111111111111111 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ChatGPT <chatgpt@example.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Apr 2026 00:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] sched/cpufreq: add Snowflake governor for pissarro

Add a schedutil-class CPUFreq governor named "snowflake" for the
Pissarro/MT6877 Android 4.14 kernel tree.

Snowflake keeps the scheduler-driven cpufreq_update_util() path, WALT/uclamp
utilization, iowait boost, fast/slow switch handling, and the MTK SSPM cluster
frequency path used by the existing schedutil implementation. It adds a small
set of Android-friendly tunables for fast foreground ramp-up, slower decay and
moderate frame-stability boost without forcing maximum clocks.

Signed-off-by: ChatGPT <chatgpt@example.com>
---
 Documentation/snowflake-cpufreq.txt   |   36 +
 arch/arm64/configs/pissarro_defconfig |    4 +
 drivers/cpufreq/Kconfig               |   31 +
 kernel/sched/Makefile                 |    1 +
 kernel/sched/cpufreq_snowflake.c      | 1080 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 5 files changed, 1151 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
