diff --git a/Documentation/snowflake-cpufreq.txt b/Documentation/snowflake-cpufreq.txt
new file mode 100644
index 000000000000..111111111111
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Documentation/snowflake-cpufreq.txt
@@ -0,0 +1,36 @@
+Snowflake CPUFreq governor for Pissarro / MT6877
+==================================================
+
+Snowflake is a schedutil-class governor named "snowflake". It is intended for
+Android 4.14 MTK non-GKI trees where schedutil already drives DVFS through
+scheduler utilization callbacks.
+
+Design goals:
+
+  - keep the proven schedutil update path, WALT/uclamp accounting and MTK SSPM
+    cluster frequency route used by this tree;
+  - ramp up quickly enough for foreground frame stability;
+  - decay more slowly to avoid frequency oscillation and frame-time spikes;
+  - use small utilization boosts instead of forcing maximum clocks.
+
+Default tunables are exposed under each CPUFreq policy, for example:
+
+  /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpufreq/policy0/snowflake/up_rate_limit_us
+  /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpufreq/policy0/snowflake/down_rate_limit_us
+  /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpufreq/policy0/snowflake/target_load
+  /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpufreq/policy0/snowflake/hispeed_load
+  /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpufreq/policy0/snowflake/hispeed_freq
+  /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpufreq/policy0/snowflake/boost_pct
+  /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpufreq/policy0/snowflake/iowait_boost_enable
+  /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpufreq/policy0/snowflake/busy_hold_enable
+  /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpufreq/policy0/snowflake/rt_dl_boost_enable
+
+Balanced starting point for Pissarro:
+
+  echo 500 > policy*/snowflake/up_rate_limit_us
+  echo 16000 > policy*/snowflake/down_rate_limit_us
+  echo 80 > policy*/snowflake/target_load
+  echo 90 > policy*/snowflake/hispeed_load
+  echo 2 > policy*/snowflake/boost_pct
+
+The governor intentionally does not bypass thermal, battery or policy limits.

